{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `pass3_over_findings`) is deterministic; every input is in the v2 sidecar (`sidecar.py:702-703` persists per-finding `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` losslessly). `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` proves the replay works but is a one-off script with hardcoded baselines.\n\n`orchestrator.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, *, execution_review=False)` (`orchestrator.py:662-711`) is the REAL LIVE path: `_threshold_for` special-cases `\"prerequisite-consistency\" -> (0.60, True)`, else resolves live via `_criteria.threshold_for(criteria, crit_by_id, gate=\"plan_review\")` (`crit_by_id = registry.by_id()`), bumps `block_threshold = max(bt, 0.80)` when `execution_review and blocking_enabled`; applies `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` (forces `\"na\"` for findings whose criteria miss `registry.CODEBASE_GROUNDED`) before `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings(..., threshold_for=_threshold_for, impact_fn=review_kernel.impact_plan, execution_review=...)`.\n\n**Registry drift is distinct from `impact_model_version`.** Thresholds live in `criteria_routing.json`, governed by `regver`. Comparing live-resolved thresholds against a stored decision flips whenever `regver` moved, even with `impact_model_version` unchanged. Tier-0 computes THREE things per finding:\n\n1. **stored** — the sidecar's decision.\n2. **replayed-stored** — `pass3_decide` fed the PERSISTED `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` (no re-resolution) — harness self-check; MUST always equal `stored`.\n3. **live-baseline** — `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (live-resolved) — may legitimately differ from `stored` on registry drift.\n\n**Candidate** (`--candidate <name>`) is diffed against **live-baseline** — Tier-0's purpose. Resolved via `candidates/__init__.py`'s `CANDIDATES: dict[str, Candidate]` (`overlay: dict[str, tuple[float, bool]]` per-criterion override, `impact_fn: Callable = review_kernel.impact_plan`). `\"current\"` is built-in (empty overlay, default `impact_fn`). Candidate's `threshold_for` mirrors `_threshold_for` against the overlay; `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` applied identically; then `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings(..., threshold_for=<mirrored>, impact_fn=<candidate's>, execution_review=...)`.\n\n`corpus.build_corpus`'s cache rows are summary-only; `findings`/`verification` need the SAME re-read `labels.py` uses: `_enumerate_event_blobs` + `_batch_cat` matched by `review_event_uuid`, then `data[\"findings\"]`.\n\n**Plan-v4->v5 baseline, made importable.** `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py:162` `legacy_impact_plan`: shipped `impact_plan` scores pre-v5 ordinal grades as 0.0, collapsing the baseline — the script pins `legacy_impact_plan` (line 272) as the PRE-v5 baseline. `docs/calibration/` has NO `__init__.py`, not import-path-reachable, so `legacy_impact_plan`/`classify`/`RULES` (lines 124-162) move verbatim into a NEW `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py`; the doc script imports them from there (no duplication). AC2 imports from the new module, pairing `classify`/`RULES` with `legacy_impact_plan` for that one comparison; every other comparison uses `review_kernel.impact_plan`.\n\nTicket-level labels (`labels.py`, closed) need `show_ticket` per ticket — too slow at full-corpus scale. Label-proxy metrics: SEPARATE, OPTIONAL, only over a supplied `labels-<hash>.jsonl`; report states coverage fraction.\n\n**Friction rate**, defined: `count(findings where live-baseline decision is non-blocking AND candidate decision is blocking) / count(all findings scored)` — i.e. the fraction of the scored corpus the candidate would newly block that current production would not. Computed over ALL scored findings (not only grounded ones); a companion count in the other direction (candidate unblocks a live-baseline block) is reported separately as \"relief count\", not folded into friction rate.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (+ `legacy_v4_baseline.py`, `candidates/__init__.py`, `report.py`, `__main__.py`):\n\n- Extract `classify`/`RULES`/`legacy_impact_plan` from `plan_v5_rescore.py` into `legacy_v4_baseline.py`; update the doc script to import from there.\n- Input: corpus, OPTIONAL `labels_path`, `--candidate <name>` via `candidates.CANDIDATES[name]` (`KeyError` -> clear error listing known names).\n- Full-body re-read per row via `_enumerate_event_blobs`/`_batch_cat`; `data[\"findings\"]` + per-index persisted thresholds + `verification` feed Pass-3.\n- `__main__.py`: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate <name> [--labels <path>]`.\n- Per finding compute `stored`, `replayed-stored` (`pass3_decide` w/ persisted thresholds only — assert-equal to `stored`, not reported as a \"flip\"), `live-baseline`, `candidate`.\n- AC2: `legacy_v4_baseline.classify`/`RULES` mapping vs `legacy_v4_baseline.legacy_impact_plan`.\n- Report: flip matrix — (a) `stored` vs `live-baseline` = registry-drift count, (b) `live-baseline` vs `candidate` = candidate-induced flips (primary signal); friction rate (formula above) + relief count; per-criterion deltas; priority shift. IF `labels_path`: label-proxy metrics + coverage fraction; ELSE states not computed.\n- Post-verdict floors replayed only when inputs present; otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py` (new — relocated from `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py`)\n- `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` (edited — imports from the new module)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/candidates/__init__.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: `replayed-stored` exactly equals `stored` for every fixture finding; a fixture with a registry threshold differing from its persisted `block_threshold` shows `live-baseline` != `stored` while `replayed-stored` still == `stored`; candidate `\"current\"` == `live-baseline`; an overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the boundary findings; friction rate computed correctly against a fixture with a known ratio of newly-blocked findings; `prerequisite-consistency` special case and `execution_review` bump each exercised once; unknown `--candidate` raises a clear error; v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` skipped and counted; pre-v5 graded row classified via `legacy_v4_baseline.classify` vs `legacy_impact_plan`; `plan_v5_rescore.py` still runs post-extraction; label-proxy metrics omitted without `labels_path`; `__main__.py` subcommand dispatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero `replayed-stored` vs `stored` mismatches for every finding; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4->plan-v5 change (via the relocated `legacy_v4_baseline` module) reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report separately states registry-drift flips (`stored` vs `live-baseline`) and candidate-induced flips (`live-baseline` vs `candidate`), plus friction rate (per the formula above) and per-criterion deltas; checked by inspection.\n- [ ] IF a labels file is supplied, the report additionally contains label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction, annotated against the noise band; checked by inspection when available.\n- [ ] The Pass-3 replay itself (excluding any optional label-proxy step) completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop over the real corpus, with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and no provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788087653812773081,"uuid":"17070043-ef90-4fe3-a91a-91ec358bc493"}